# Project Context

This is a computer vision + AI demo project for a computer vision/AI consulting portfolio. The purpose is to create an impressive portfolio project that will help landing clients in Upwork and other freelancing platforms (the target clients need computer vision+ machine learning +Agentic AI services), as well as to help land machine learning + computer vision +Agenic AI jobs

## What it does
Detects surface defects on steel (NEU-DET dataset) using a fine-tuned YOLO11 
model, then sends the cropped defect region to a vision-capable LLM 
(GPT-4o-mini or Claude) to generate a natural language description, severity 
assessment, and recommended action.

## Approach
- YOLO11 fine-tuned via transfer learning from a COCO-pretrained checkpoint
- Annotations converted from PASCAL VOC/XML to YOLO format via a custom script
- VLM step uses a hosted multimodal LLM API (no local hosting required)

## Structure
- /data — NEU-DET dataset (gitignored, from Kaggle "NEU Surface Defect Database")
- /models — trained YOLO weights (gitignored, hosted on Hugging Face for reuse)
- /src — core logic: annotation conversion, training, inference pipeline, VLM wrapper
- /api — FastAPI backend, single endpoint takes image, returns report
- /frontend — simple HTML/CSS/JS UI: upload image, see annotated result + report

## Image Processing
- Preprocessing: apply CLAHE (contrast-limited adaptive histogram equalization) 
  to input images before YOLO inference — improves detection on low-contrast 
  steel surface defects
- Post-processing: use OpenCV to draw annotated bounding boxes on output images, 
  and to crop detected defect regions (with padding) before sending to VLM
- Document both in README as deliberate engineering choices, not just plumbing

## Goals
- Clean, production-quality code (this will be public on GitHub for portfolio/job applications)
- Keep it simple — this is a demo, not a full product
- API keys go in .env, never hardcoded
- Commit incrementally — real development history, not one final dump

## Stack
Python, Ultralytics YOLO11, FastAPI, vanilla JS frontend, OpenAI/Anthropic API for VLM